%description:

A deviation of StochasticChannelModel::getAttenuation() from the specification,
recorded rather than fixed (tests/doc/model-deviations.md, item 15): the building
penetration loss of a D2D link between an indoor and an outdoor UE depends on which
of the two transmits.

TR 36.843 V12.0.0 A.2.1.2, "Channel models":

    Following channel models shall be used for D2D.

    Outdoor to Outdoor    Outdoor to Indoor    Indoor to Indoor

with, in the row "Pathloss", the column "Outdoor to Indoor" (for "Remaining Layout
Options"):

    LOS: PL_B1_tot (dout + din) + 20.0 + 0.5*d_in

    NLOS: PL_B1_tot(dout + din) + 20.0 + 0.5*din - 0.8*h_MS

where the first column has "d is distance between UEs". So the table has a model per
pair of environments, with no column for an indoor UE transmitting to an outdoor
one, and no term that tells the transmitter from the receiver: a link with one
indoor end has one wall, whichever way the frame goes. The model takes the state of
the receiving end, so A indoors, B outdoors gives no wall on A -> B and the full
wall on B -> A.

The checks say that the two directions are equal, and that each has the wall of the
LOS formula above: 20.0 + 0.5*d_in over the outdoor path loss. The model's outdoor
path loss differs from PL_B1_tot (item 4), which is not at issue here, so the wall is
measured against the same link with both ends outdoors. Checked at 2 GHz on a fixed
LOS link, 100 m between the UEs, with shadowing and fading off.

ChannelModelD2dIndoorDirection pins what the model does today, so that any change to
it fails there by name. When the model follows the specification, drop that pin and
this test's line of expected failure.

%expected-failure: a D2D link with one indoor end has the wall in one direction only, not in both (TR 36.843 A.2.1.2; model-deviations item 15)

%includes:
#include <cmath>
#include "SchedulerTestUtil.h"
#include "ChannelModelTestUtil.h"

%global:
using namespace simu5g;
using namespace simu5g::unittest;
using inet::Coord;

// The model's own D2D link builder, which is protected. Never instantiated: see ChannelModelProbe for the technique.
struct D2dLinkAccess : StochasticChannelModel
{
    static auto d2dLinkPtr() { return &D2dLinkAccess::d2dLink; }
};

%file: harness.ned
import simu5g.common.binder.Binder;
import simu5g.stack.phy.medium.CellularRadioMedium;
import simu5g.common.carrierAggregation.CarrierAggregation;
import simu5g.stack.phy.channelmodel.Tr38901ChannelModel;

network Harness
{
    submodules:
        binder: Binder;
        radioMedium: CellularRadioMedium;
        carrierAggregation: CarrierAggregation;
        model: Tr38901ChannelModel;
        test: Test;
}

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
network = Harness
cmdenv-express-mode = false
cmdenv-log-prefix = ""
sim-time-limit = 1s

*.carrierAggregation.numComponentCarriers = 1
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].carrierFrequency = 2GHz
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].numBands = 4
**.componentCarrierModule = "carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0]"
**.cellInfoModule = ""
*.binder.printTrafficGeneratorConfig = false

**.scenario = "URBAN_MICROCELL"
**.nodebHeight = 10m
**.ueHeight = 1.5m
**.dynamicLos = false
**.fixedLos = true
**.shadowing = false
**.fading = false

%no-default-inifile: 1

%activity:
Checker c;
auto *medium = harnessModule<CellularRadioMedium>(this, "radioMedium");
auto *model = harnessModule<StochasticChannelModel>(this, "model");

StubEndpoint a, b;
a.nodeId = MacNodeId(1025);
b.nodeId = MacNodeId(1026);
a.coord = Coord(0, 0, 1.5);
b.coord = Coord(60, 80, 1.5);
StubRadioRegistration aRadio(medium, a.nodeId, &a);
StubRadioRegistration bRadio(medium, b.nodeId, &b);

auto attenuation = [&] (StubEndpoint& from, StubEndpoint& to) {
    return model->getAttenuation((model->*D2dLinkAccess::d2dLinkPtr())(from.nodeId, from.coord, to.nodeId, to.coord));
};

wait(SimTime(10, SIMTIME_MS));

const double outdoors = attenuation(a, b);
a.insideBuilding = true;
a.insideDistance = 7;
const double aToB = attenuation(a, b), bToA = attenuation(b, a);

c.expectNear("a link with one indoor end has the same path loss in both directions", aToB, bToA, 1e-9);
c.expectNear("the indoor UE sending has the wall, 20.0 + 0.5*d_in", aToB - outdoors, 23.5, 1e-9);
c.expectNear("the indoor UE receiving has the wall, 20.0 + 0.5*d_in", bToA - outdoors, 23.5, 1e-9);

c.summary();

%contains: stdout
modelchecks=3 modelfailures=0

%not-contains: stdout
FAILED
